  <div class="connection" class:offline={!endpoint}><span class="light"></span><div><strong>{endpoint ? 'CTG MCP is running' : 'MCP is unavailable'}</strong><p>{endpoint ?? editor.environment?.mcp_error ?? 'Waiting for the engine…'}</p></div><span class="tag">37 TOOLS</span></div>
  <div class="connect-grid"><article><h2>01 / CONNECT YOUR CLIENT</h2><p>Add this streamable HTTP server to your client's MCP configuration. Client-specific configuration formats may differ.</p><pre>{config}</pre><button onclick={() => void copy()}>{copied ? 'Copied configuration' : 'Copy configuration'}</button><p class="caption">CTG must stay open. The server is available on this computer only.</p></article>
  <article><h2>02 / GIVE IT A MUSICAL IDEA</h2><blockquote>“Compose an original emotional funk song. Write a memorable melody and an answering phrase. Use warm keys and a rubber bass. Build a quiet bridge, then bring the hook back. Save the project and render a WAV.”</blockquote><p>The AI can write every note directly. It doesn't have to use the random-song generator.</p><div class="tools"><span>pattern_create</span><span>instrument_update</span><span>arrangement_place_many</span><span>export_wav</span></div></article></div>
  <div class="connection-note"><strong>Your session stays editable.</strong><span>AI changes appear in the undo history. Projects and exports live in {editor.environment?.workspace ?? 'your Music folder'}. No built-in AI subscription or cloud synthesis is required; bring your own MCP client.</span></div>
